cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Session-level evaluation protocol and audit tools for the durian
  disease benchmark
message: >-
  If you use this software or the accompanying dataset, please cite
  both. The dataset DOI below is the one to cite for the images and
  the capture-session identifiers.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lin
    given-names: Ding Shan
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0009-6031-8479
    affiliation: UCSI University
repository-code: https://github.com/xiaolin200206/durian-session-benchmark
url: https://github.com/xiaolin200206/durian-session-benchmark
abstract: >-
  Training, evaluation and audit code for a durian disease dataset
  collected in Peninsular Malaysia. The 560 images resolve into 73
  independent capture sessions; an image-level random split places
  79.6% of images in sessions that straddle the train-test boundary
  and inflates macro F1 by 12.2 points on average across nine
  architectures. This repository contains the partitioning utilities
  that avoid that, and a script for each of the four protocol
  decisions the accompanying paper measures.
keywords:
  - data leakage
  - grouped cross-validation
  - capture session
  - plant disease classification
  - reproducibility
  - benchmark
